Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
The 3+1 super-loop: the symbols and the programs of Test 2 in the Wolfram \
Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"57b8c8f6-8306-45ef-8efa-e735fe69b871"],

Cell["\<\
PROJECT spacetimes. Notebook 3+1super-loop.nb, prepared for Patrick Lee Nash, \
Ph.D.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"537b7fbb-43cb-4e69-b520-cc5d761580c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook is written for a physics student who has not seen the work \
before. It does two things. Part I gives every symbol of the project a \
Wolfram Language form that looks exactly like the printed symbol (for example \
",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "LL", "vac"], TraditionalForm]], 
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b4291944-b108-45e7-8cf9-339e879219f3"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"71adb4a0-ca05-4d87-ade7-cf453681cd37"],
 ", the gap of the condensed vacuum) and behaves as one indivisible symbol in \
computations; it then checks this with computations that use sums, arithmetic \
and algebra. Part II (added in later stages) collects, as an encyclopedia, \
every program of Test 2, rewritten in the Wolfram Language, with every check \
of the original programs."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c07dec2-08da-400a-a055-51270592725a"],

Cell["\<\
How to use it. Open the notebook in Wolfram (version 15 or later; it was \
evaluated with Wolfram 15.0.1) and choose Evaluation > Evaluate Notebook. \
Every cell is evaluated in order; every test prints PASS or FAIL, and the \
last cell of each part lists all tests. Nothing outside this notebook is \
read: the registry of the symbols and all programs are inside it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eafb4e0f-b3cc-48ab-84a5-e8ff5fde7322"],

Cell["\<\
How to read it. Text cells explain, in words, what the next input cell does \
and why. Inside the code, comments (* like this *) explain each step. Every \
symbol of the physics is written with its printed form; every Wolfram \
Language function that is used is named in the text the first time it appears.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2e378c1-3903-44f0-b4b0-b8d2996233c9"],

Cell["Part I. The symbols", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"97d32b61-4c97-4e4d-be91-756a5e351bba"],

Cell["I.1 Why every symbol of the project carries the suffix LL", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ca6f5975-7bd5-4186-a5bf-6121e5f0a6ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Papers and notebooks in physics often use one letter for several different \
objects: ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox["\[CapitalDelta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"6121f95a-d416-4577-b80f-c925e38e20d8"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4132cbaa-1765-4201-af2c-71fcd5055e1a"],
 " may be a gap, a Laplacian or a difference; ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "ebefb124-2c7b-4c13-a986-d6fcc3770372"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9991f470-c89b-4dfb-a492-7eed150e575c"],
 " a mass or an index. In a long project with many documents and programs \
this produces errors that are hard to find. The project therefore keeps a \
registry: every symbol that it creates has a unique printed form, and the \
symbols of the super-loop revision carry the suffix LL, in a subscript or \
superscript (for example ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["G", "TI"], "LL"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"6a3580ee-2847-4b05-ad7a-5d9a2c639eb5"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5ccaebf1-bb0d-4c7c-90c9-ce6424242ca2"],
 ", the coupling of the contact interaction, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Tau]", "\[Iota]", "LL"], TraditionalForm]], 
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f3e36fc8-ec53-4dc4-8aa9-0869ca427136"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"18ffbdc1-8920-4174-84b1-4ac700fabcec"],
 ", the Pauli matrices of isospin). The registry lists for each symbol its \
printed form (written in TeX), its plain-text names (the names under which \
programs and data files write it), its meaning and its origin. Part I brings \
this whole registry into the Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca32b865-546e-40b0-b4f3-8b4ef005113f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the Wolfram Language an ordinary subscript is not a symbol: the input ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "LL"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"6c12110e-7482-4fcc-9356-6400047f1ce6"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d5cf2fe8-7a02-43fa-8d76-64ee644acacf"],
 " is the expression ",
 StyleBox["Subscript[a, LL]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", a function of two symbols. One cannot safely give it a value, and it can \
be confused with other subscripted expressions. Part I uses the Notation \
package, which is part of every Wolfram installation, to turn each printed \
form into one indivisible symbol (a \"symbolized\" symbol)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2fa4b8e-c08d-4973-b1f7-07dc1e10a2f0"],

Cell["I.2 The technique: symbolized symbols, created by a program", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"af15044b-c71d-42c4-95bc-78563f90015d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Notation package works on boxes, the structures that describe how an \
input looks on the screen. The two-dimensional input ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "LL"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"90219eee-6e7b-41f6-a110-b2fba30803d2"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"903423c7-821c-4fe6-9592-28fb9fabf917"],
 " is the box ",
 StyleBox["SubscriptBox[\"a\", \"LL\"]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ". The command ",
 StyleBox["Symbolize[ParsedBoxWrapper[box], WorkingForm -> StandardForm]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " tells the Wolfram Language: whenever an input contains exactly this box, \
read it as one new symbol, and whenever that symbol is printed, print it as \
this box. The wrapper ",
 StyleBox["ParsedBoxWrapper",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " marks its argument as a box structure (this is the way to call ",
 StyleBox["Symbolize",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " from a program; the palette of the package inserts an equivalent wrapper \
when one works by hand)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0453b9aa-97d8-48e0-ab29-69201f94a135"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The option ",
 StyleBox["WorkingForm -> StandardForm",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " is essential here. Without it the package asks the front end for the \
format of the notebook in which the input was typed (",
 StyleBox["InputNotebook[]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "). When a notebook is evaluated by a program, or when no notebook is \
selected, there is no such notebook, the answer is ",
 StyleBox["$Failed",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", and the package stores its reading rule for the format ",
 StyleBox["$Failed",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ": the symbol is created but the input box is never recognized. This was \
found while this notebook was being prepared: the tests below failed until \
the option was given explicitly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a9e896c5-d2e7-491d-8f69-7779f79bd374"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next cell loads the package and symbolizes one example, ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "LL"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"12e4ef5d-cb75-4993-a09f-dab767d5d456"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"791f245d-2a27-4a63-a013-44a373aefb06"],
 ". The cells after it show that the two-dimensional input is now one symbol, \
that it can receive a value, and how a program reaches the symbol from its \
box: ",
 StyleBox["MakeExpression[box, StandardForm]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " reads a box the same way the notebook reads input, and returns the result \
wrapped in ",
 StyleBox["HoldComplete",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (so that it is not evaluated)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14717feb-ea8c-4e25-96d0-af056d5356e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"load", " ", "the", " ", "Notation", " ", "package", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
     "it", " ", "ships", " ", "with", " ", "every", " ", "Wolfram", " ", 
      "installation"}], ")"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Notation`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
    "create", " ", "the", " ", "symbol", " ", "a_LL", " ", "from", " ", "the",
      " ", "box", " ", "\"\<a with the subscript LL\>\""}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Symbolize", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ParsedBoxWrapper", "[", 
       RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"WorkingForm", " ", "->", " ", "StandardForm"}]}], "]"}], ";"}],
    "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
    "the", " ", "name", " ", "that", " ", "the", " ", "package", " ", "gave", 
     " ", "to", " ", "the", " ", "new", " ", "symbol", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
      "the", " ", "separator", " ", "is", " ", "the", " ", "character", " ", 
       "\[UnderBracket]"}], ")"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
   "Names", "[", "\"\<Global`a\[UnderBracket]*\>\"", "]"}]}]}]], "Input",Expre\
ssionUUID->"65e925da-4db3-4c2f-a9dd-937ed0cc8a14"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"the", " ", "box", " ", "of", " ", "a_LL"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"read", " ", "as", " ", "input"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"is", " ", "now", " ", "ONE", " ", 
     RowBox[{"symbol", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "its", " ", "head", " ", "is", " ", "Symbol", " ", "and", " ", "it", " ",
        "is", " ", "an", " ", "atom"}]}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"h", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"MakeExpression", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "StandardForm"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"h", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Head", " ", "@@", " ", "h"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AtomQ", " ", "@@", " ", "h"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",Exp\
ressionUUID->"f172fb24-ddfe-4efa-ba00-9de71685008e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ordinary expression ",
 StyleBox["Subscript[a, LL]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", typed as text, is NOT the symbol: only the box is symbolized. A program \
therefore reaches a symbolized symbol through its box, with ",
 StyleBox["MakeExpression",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", which returns ",
 StyleBox["HoldComplete[symbol]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ". To give it a value, the held symbol is put into an assignment with ",
 StyleBox["Apply",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (written ",
 StyleBox["@@",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "): ",
 StyleBox["Set @@ HoldComplete[symbol, value]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " replaces the head ",
 StyleBox["HoldComplete",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " by ",
 StyleBox["Set",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and gives ",
 StyleBox["Set[symbol, value]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "; because ",
 StyleBox["Set",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " does not evaluate its first argument, the symbol itself (and not its old \
value) receives the value. In the same way ",
 StyleBox["Clear @@ HoldComplete[symbol]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " gives ",
 StyleBox["Clear[symbol]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7653c70-6454-48f0-9c95-824878c17e76"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"the", " ", "text", " ", "input", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "LL"}], "]"}], " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", 
     "compound", " ", "expression"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"not", " ", "the", " ", "symbol"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "LL"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"AtomQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "LL"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",Express\
ionUUID->"36df0ea0-94f0-4ef4-bb34-6d19535c6399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
    "assign", " ", "the", " ", "value", " ", "42", " ", "to", " ", "the", " ",
      "symbol", " ", "a_LL", " ", "through", " ", "its", " ", "box"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"then", " ", "read", " ", "it", " ", 
     RowBox[{"back", ":", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"HoldComplete", "[", "a_LL", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"HoldComplete", "[", "42", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "is", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldComplete", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a_LL", ",", " ", "42"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"and", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Set", " ", "@@"}]}], " ", "..."}], " ", "is", " ", "a_LL"}], 
     " ", "=", " ", "42"}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"MakeExpression", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          "StandardForm"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"Set", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
        RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"HoldComplete", "[", "42", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ";"}], 
   "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ReleaseHold", "[", 
     RowBox[{"MakeExpression", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       "StandardForm"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}]}]], "Input",Expr\
essionUUID->"3e118c12-da80-4809-92b5-752b6e305e0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"remove", " ", "the", " ", "value", " ", "again"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
    "so", " ", "that", " ", "a_LL", " ", "is", " ", "a", " ", "free", " ", 
     "symbol", " ", "for", " ", "the", " ", "rest", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", 
     RowBox[{"notebook", ":", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "@@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"HoldComplete", "[", "a_LL", "]"}]}], " ", "is", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Clear", "[", "a_LL", "]"}]}]}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"MakeExpression", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          "StandardForm"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Clear", " ", "@@", " ", "s"}]}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"ReleaseHold", "[", 
    RowBox[{"MakeExpression", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<LL\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "StandardForm"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f00be8ba-\
53cb-485e-8d11-710abc51c48e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A symbolized symbol is one indivisible atom: the letters inside its scripts \
are not separate symbols. The next cell shows this with the symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"LL", ",", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"b221aa24-57e6-4c9a-942e-2a98c1bc7100"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b3dcfd0d-5b7d-402a-b0ed-bb5df48f333d"],
 ", whose subscript holds the label LL and the index letter ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "60a29333-5b48-409c-ac74-770ae38c00d7"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fa55ca86-57bc-4ff6-9dd1-5e170ed649fd"],
 ". In a sum whose summation variable is also called ",
 StyleBox["LL",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", the whole symbol is multiplied by the summation variable, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{"LL", "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], "2",
      LimitsPositioning->True], "LL", " ", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"LL", ",", 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{"3", " "}], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"LL", ",", 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"dcb2e14a-2672-42c1-bfd3-90e57be0bdf6"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"06faa2e4-06a8-4c08-9dd8-d36a7c459faa"],
 ": the LL inside the subscript is untouched. For comparison, the ordinary \
subscripted expression ",
 StyleBox["Subscript[b, LL, p]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", which is not symbolized, is a compound expression in which ",
 StyleBox["LL",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " is replaced: its sum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", " "}], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"63126107-077d-4b53-99bb-a87b955d154f"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e71e2af0-998f-41d7-ac9f-b86b337926f5"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a295ec83-2c3b-4c20-b005-c41ff05717e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One rule must be observed when a box is symbolized by a program: the box \
must be exactly the box that the front end sends to the kernel when the \
symbol is typed. Before an input cell is evaluated, the front end reads every \
string of its boxes again, as typed text, and cuts it into tokens: names (a \
letter followed by letters and digits), numbers and single other characters. \
The subscript of a typed ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"LL", ",", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"1a6c4497-61bf-4012-b5ba-2a0a4e2247d8"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2c812c2f-0b88-4c37-8aba-c937d0739c05"],
 " therefore arrives as ",
 StyleBox["RowBox[{\"LL\", \",\", \"p\"}]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", three tokens. A box written by hand as ",
 StyleBox["SubscriptBox[\"a\", \"LL,p\"]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", with the whole subscript in one string, is never matched by typed input, \
because the front end never sends that string. This was found while the \
notebook was prepared (a test notebook, evaluated in the front end, showed \
exactly this), and the converter of section I.3 builds the cut form."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea3b293e-210d-4132-a2ca-bd4131aa2144"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"symbolize", " ", "a_", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}], "}"}]}], ":", " ", 
     RowBox[{
     "the", " ", "subscript", " ", "\"\<LL, p\>\"", " ", "exactly", " ", "as",
       " ", "the", " ", "front", " ", "end", " ", "stores", " ", "it"}]}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"three", " ", "tokens", " ", "in", " ", "a", " ", "RowBox"}]}], 
   " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Symbolize", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ParsedBoxWrapper", "[", 
       RowBox[{"SubscriptBox", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"RowBox", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<LL\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<,\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<p\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"WorkingForm", " ", "->", " ", "StandardForm"}]}], "]"}], ";"}],
    "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
      "the", " ", "summation", " ", "variable", " ", "is", " ", "called", " ",
        "LL"}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"the", " ", "symbol", " ", "a_", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}], "}"}], " ", "is", " ", "one", " ", 
       "atom"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
     "so", " ", "its", " ", "subscript", " ", "is", " ", "untouched"}]}], " ",
     "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"LL", " ", 
      SubscriptBox["a", 
       RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}]]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"LL", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"the", " ", "same", " ", "sum"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"compared", " ", "with", " ", "3", " ", "a_", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}], "}"}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["a", 
      RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}]]}], " ", "===", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"LL", " ", 
       SubscriptBox["a", 
        RowBox[{"LL", ",", "p"}]]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"LL", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"the", " ", "ordinary"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"NOT", " ", "symbolized"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"subscripted", " ", 
      RowBox[{"expression", ":", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "here", " ", "LL", " ", "is", " ", "replaced", " ", "by", " ", "1", " ",
         "and", " ", "2"}]}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
   RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"LL", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", "LL", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"LL", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"72158593-98e5-4086-95a8-\
0666e389a280"],

