Cell["I.3 From the printed form (TeX) to boxes", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"100ae07c-9a20-4d84-bba4-98bb72823c40"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The registry stores every symbol in TeX, the language in which the \
documents of the project are typeset; for example the gap of the condensed \
vacuum is ",
 StyleBox["\\Delta^{\\rm vac}_{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ". The next cell defines, in the context SL31, a small reader of exactly \
this kind of TeX. It splits the TeX into tokens, reads them from left to \
right, and builds the box. A command such as ",
 StyleBox["\\Delta",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " becomes the Greek letter; ",
 StyleBox["^{...}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["_{...}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " become a superscript and a subscript; ",
 StyleBox["{\\rm LL}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " becomes the upright text LL (roman text that holds several tokens, such as \
",
 StyleBox["{\\rm int,F}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["{\\rm s(2)}",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", is cut into tokens exactly as the front end cuts typed text, section \
I.2); ",
 StyleBox["\\vec d",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " becomes a d with an arrow. Letters in special alphabets keep their \
alphabet: double-struck (",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "474ead15-538e-45bc-879c-d4128615b94b"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1f5ec909-b031-4b37-8124-2d8dbc4656e2"],
 "), script (",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "77113327-25b1-4f20-b370-cb95308a9d92"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "28d8c53b-59b4-43d6-9829-4b35903895b0"],
 ") and Gothic (",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "9972179e-80be-4821-ba4c-98d189e98cd1"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8e2dcfa1-2ae5-4709-aef3-6e3d0703f978"],
 ") letters are separate characters of the Wolfram Language, and sans-serif (",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["N",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "d61f05cf-3695-4be7-93e2-6cbc39eadf0d"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ec6facf6-01e5-42b0-8495-6ef5d76e30e6"],
 ") and bold (",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    StyleBox["x",
     FontSlant->"Bold"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "e14fb5ea-49ad-4f20-8ae0-4e4add120f28"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "41f9fd55-8081-4e77-a821-b98bbc281934"],
 ") letters are wrapped in a ",
 StyleBox["TagBox",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", which the Notation package does not remove when it compares boxes, so \
that a bold, a sans-serif and an ordinary letter with the same scripts remain \
three different symbols."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b26e8b3f-7c83-4db1-a972-f8652125ab9c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same cell defines the functions that split an entry of the registry \
into single symbols, classify every item (a symbol, a family of symbols with \
running indices, a function symbol, a group, an index, an operator, and so \
on), give every symbolized symbol a readable name, symbolize it, and reach it \
by its TeX: ",
 StyleBox["LL[tex]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " returns the symbol of the TeX item ",
 StyleBox["tex",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["LL[tex, index -> value]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " the symbol of one of its components. In the input cells of this notebook \
the symbols appear directly in their printed form."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"912b1ff3-78b9-4262-91af-61b6ab78c865"],

